{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"server side paging server side paging","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md","fileName":"Server-Side Paging.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Server-Side Paging","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Web Data Query and Presentation]], [[Web Performance and Scalability]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Data Query and Presentation","Web Performance and Scalability","HTTP Request","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"server side paging server side paging","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md","fileName":"Server-Side Paging.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Server-Side Paging","heading":"Server-Side Paging","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Server-side paging applies a page index and page size to a query before the result crosses the API boundary. The response returns only the requested records together with enough metadata, such as a total count, for the client to render navigation.\n\nIt reduces database materialization, network transfer, and browser rendering for large datasets. Page changes require new [[HTTP Request|requests]], so sorting and filtering parameters must be sent with the page selection.\n\nFor a high-demand API, paging also bounds the work performed by any one collection request. The page size remains a capacity choice: a value that is too large loses the protection, while one that is too small creates excess navigation and request traffic.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Data Query and Presentation","Web Performance and Scalability","HTTP Request","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"server side paging server side paging","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Server-Side Paging.md","fileName":"Server-Side Paging.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Server-Side Paging","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf]]\n[[aspnetcore3andreact.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Data Query and Presentation","Web Performance and Scalability","HTTP Request","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}